    "narrative": "For August 22, the Austin Waves lineup is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (66.87) and **Coby Mayo** (62.51), who both benefit significantly from a favorable park environment and a exploitable matchup against Shane McClanahan. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a priority start despite a neutral platoon split, as his high-ceiling production makes him our most efficient asset today. **Liam Hicks** (59.92) also emerges as a high-value play; despite hitting lower in the order, his efficiency score is buoyed by an excellent park factor and a favorable matchup against Brandon Young, providing a rare \"Strong\" rating from the bottom of the lineup.\n\nWhile our starting outfield is deep, **Jackson Merrill** (58.97) remains a high-priority piece due to his elite SB potential, though he takes a slight efficiency hit for the matchup against Dean Kremer. Conversely, **Heliot Ramos** (46.34) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. Although **Heliot Ramos** offers favorable stolen base upside against a slower pitcher like Dylan Cease, his overall efficiency score fell just short of the current outfield rotation, which prioritizes the high-base projections of players like **Kyle Tucker** (58.11) and **Andy Pages** (53.68).\n\nRisks for today center on the \"Lineup Pending\" status of several starters, including **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci**, whose projections rely on estimated spot-in-order data. **Drake Baldwin** faces a particularly difficult assignment against the elite arm of Logan Henderson, keeping his score suppressed near the floor for a starting catcher. We are also closely monitoring **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.99), whose power profile against Luis Castillo is hampered by a significant platoon disadvantage. We will finalize these slots once official lineups are posted to ensure no caps are wasted on players relegated to bench roles.",
